WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
Hey Henry, can you bite my finger please?

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:03.820
Bite my finger

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:08.520
Henry, we're never gonna go viral unless you bite my finger!

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:11.180
Henry says, "Good morning Uncle Hank, it's Monday!"

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:13.420
Henry, do you know how I can tell you're an astronaut?

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:19.020
Like all astronauts, you're wearing space pyjamaaaaaas!

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.760
Henry, like his father, wears pyjamas until well into the afternoon

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.280
We both work from home

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:26.660
Henry, why are you so much better lit than I am? You're stealing my light

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:32.060
You seem to have forgotten that this YouTube channel is called 'vlogbrothers' not 'vlog-adorable-baby'

00:00:32.060 --> 00:00:36.220
Having now spent 7 weeks with a newborn, I feel like I'm something of an expert in the field

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:39.200
and while babies could hardly be more adorable...

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:44.960
I can't help but come to the conclusion that babies can be a tiny bit self-centered

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:47.680
Did you just punch me in the face on purpose?

00:00:47.680 --> 00:00:53.260
It's always 'change MY diaper, feed ME, offer ME comfort, give ME a pacifier'

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:57.440
What about my pacifier Hank? When will Henry give ME a pacifier?

00:00:57.440 --> 00:01:02.200
In fact Hank, sometimes it doesn't even seem like Henry thinks I'm a person, it seems like he thinks I'm some kind of..

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:03.800
Robot-need-filler

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:08.160
*Robot voice* I am your robot-need-filler. What are your needs? Do you need to be nomed?

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:09.600
nom-nom-nom-nom-nom-nom

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:15.200
But anyway Hank, the weirdest part of the complete inability of infants to apprehend that other people also have needs

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:20.920
is that I don't care. Something weird and base and nurturing happened to me when he was born that caused me to wanna, like,

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:22.560
change poopy diapers

00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:32.880
By the way Hank, no matter how efficient a diaper changer you are, there will always be one nanosecond between the old diaper and the new diaper where the bottom is diaperless

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:35.280
and to Henry, that moment is known as

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:36.420
poopy-time

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:42.440
There's something about being a parent that that turns you weirdly insular, so you find yourself really only caring about the needs of your kid

00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:46.740
Which is why, for instance, I forgot to tell you guys that I had a book coming out in like 25 days

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:51.060
Henry says "'Will Greyson, Will Greyson  available for pre-order now! Link in the dooblydoo!"

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:52.760
Thanks bud, I appreciate the marketing

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:55.700
Hank there's this phrase in the study of religion, ultimate concern...

00:01:55.700 --> 00:02:01.660
Your ultimate concern is the thing or value that you prize above all others, the one you would die for, the one you would kill for.

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:04.780
Now, of course it's pretty easy to go through life without an ultimate concern,

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:06.680
for instance, I don't think Henry has one yet,

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:09.240
You know, because he's still in the business of self-preservation

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:11.760
But Hank, nerdfighters, that's what I want this week's theme to be,

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:15.140
Do you have an ultimate concern? What is it? Should you have one?

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:21.220
Right now, my ultimate concern certainly involves making sure that this little guy is happy and healthy and

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:24.440
has an opportunity to look at himself in various mirrors

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:29.160
But I don't know if should be limited to that. Should your ultimate concern be limited to your family?

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:35.360
Should it be about politics? or policy? about your community or your nation? Or the human species?

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:40.220
Should it take into account other species? And if so, should those species be treated as equal to humans?

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:42.620
Or should self-preservation and our own needs trump everything?

00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:46.440
and when did my husky voice transform into the voice of a pubescent boy?

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:49.760
Those are my non-rhetorical questions of the week, I'll see you on Wednesday

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:50.700
*henry sighs*

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:51.300
Ugh,

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:54.600
Did you just sigh because you're bored of me video blogging?

00:02:56.060 --> 00:02:59.180
Willie says "I'm still here! and I'm cute too!"

00:02:59.180 --> 00:03:02.240
*John sings* How we gonna kick it, gonna kick it, tummy time

00:03:02.240 --> 00:03:06.380
Yes Hank, Henry's favorite rap songs include 'how we gonna kick it, gonna kick it, tummy time',

00:03:06.380 --> 00:03:07.660
'no sleep 'till burpin',

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:10.800
and of course ' who's down with opp? dad's down with opp'

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:11.800
you know,

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:12.960
other peoples poop..

